# Release on ship

When merging work that will be (or was just) deployed to production:

1. If `CHANGELOG.md` `[Unreleased]` has entries, promote them into a new dated version section (Keep a Changelog).
2. Bump `package.json` `version` to match (patch for fixes, minor for features, major for breaking).
3. Leave an empty `## [Unreleased]` section at the top for the next work.
4. Commit the release cut (message like `Release x.y.z: promote Unreleased changelog and bump version.`) before or with the deploy.

Do not leave shipped changes sitting only under `[Unreleased]`.
